# VTID-03733 — commands actually run.

# --- Investigation --------------------------------------------------------
# Reported live: "Turkish still has English subtitles/captions under the
# orb unlike other languages." Dispatched a research agent to find the
# root cause across both vitana-v1 and vitana-platform before writing any
# code. It found: no live transcript in this widget (deliberately removed);
# the ".vtorb-status" text is a small set of fixed status phrases, resolved
# per-language via _resolveCaptionLocale()/_loc()/_caption() against a
# {en,de,es,sr,fr,pt,ru,pl,zh,ar} dictionary set — no `tr` entry anywhere,
# so every Turkish session fell through to the `en` default.

grep -n "_CAPTION_LOCALES\|_resolveCaptionLocale" \
  services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> confirmed: _CAPTION_LOCALES (the admit-list) had no 'tr'.

# Verified the true scope with two independent counts, since a naive grep
# on one quote style under-counts (some phrases use double-quoted en:/fr:
# fields because the English/French text itself contains an apostrophe):

grep -c "ar: '" services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> 42 (every phrase object's LAST field, always single-quoted — Arabic
#      text never contains a Latin apostrophe, so this is a reliable count
#      regardless of any other field's quote style)

# Confirmed the full set: _CAPTIONS (13 keys) + _DISCONNECT_LABELS (4) +
# _RECOVERY_LABELS (4) + _THINKING_QUICK(6)/_PRIMARY(7)/_ALTERNATES(8) = 42.
# Also confirmed the "thinking" filler pool (_THINKING_ALL) renders through
# the SAME _loc()/_resolveCaptionLocale() resolver as everything else
# (_setStatus(_loc(queue[0])) in _startThinkingProgress()) — so it was
# equally broken for Turkish, not just the smaller CAPTIONS/DISCONNECT/
# RECOVERY dictionaries a narrower read might have stopped at.

# --- Fix --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Wrote a small Python script (not committed — one-shot) that, for each of
# the 42 phrase objects, looked up its unique `ar:` field value in a
# hand-written EN->TR translation table and inserted `, tr: '<value>'`
# immediately after the ar: field. Chosen over 42 individual Edit calls for
# the same reason the codebase's own bulk-translation tooling exists:
# mechanical, verifiable, and the diff is trivially auditable (one `tr:`
# field appended per line, nothing else touched). Verified zero unmatched
# ar: values (42/42 matched) before writing the file.
#
# Also added 'tr' to _CAPTION_LOCALES (the resolver's admit-list) — without
# this the new translations would exist but _resolveCaptionLocale() would
# still never select them.

node -c services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> exit 0 — syntax valid. One translation (tapToHear) contains a Turkish
#      apostrophe ("Vitana'yı") — confirmed it was correctly escaped to
#      \' by the insertion script, not left as a raw quote that would have
#      broken the enclosing single-quoted string.

grep -c "tr: '" services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> 42 — matches the ar: count exactly.

# --- Cache-bust bump (CLAUDE.md IF-THEN rule 25) -----------------------------

grep -rn "orb-widget.js?v=" services/gateway/ vitana-v1/ 2>/dev/null
#   -> 4 references; 2 are dist/ build outputs (git-ignored, confirmed via
#      `git check-ignore -v`, not touched), 2 are source:
#      services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/index.html
#      vitana-v1/index.html (loads the SAME gateway-hosted script — its own
#      comment says the ?v= bump "forces browsers to refetch instead of
#      serving the cached prod widget", so both needed bumping, not just
#      the gateway repo's own Command Hub page)
# Both bumped to ?v=20260825-tr-captions.

# --- Test updates -------------------------------------------------------------
# Two existing test files independently pin the exact 10-locale shape of
# these dictionaries via strict-order regexes — both needed updating to
# 11-locale (adding `, tr: ${Q}`) or they would have failed against the fix:
#   services/gateway/test/frontend/orb-widget-caption-i18n.test.ts
#   services/gateway/test/frontend/orb-widget-thinking-messages.test.ts

cd services/gateway
npx jest --testPathPattern="orb-widget-caption-i18n|orb-widget-thinking-messages"
#   -> Test Suites: 2 passed, 2 total / Tests: 15 passed, 15 total
#   Output: outputs/targeted-tests.txt

npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> exit 0, empty output
#   Output: outputs/tsc.txt

npx jest
#   -> full gateway suite
#   Output: outputs/full-suite.txt

